---
// The masthead of the deep-dive editorial archetype: the h1, the lede under
// it, and a rule closing the block. Five routes render it — the three article
// templates, /about/ and /colophon/ — because About and Colophon are the same
// archetype as an article rather than an index (specs/routes/sitemap.md §2).
//
// Title and lede are props rather than slots because the rules they replace
// were `.article-header h1` and `.lede`: exactly one h1, exactly one lede,
// in that order, on every one of the five. A slot would let a call site put
// two headings in that position and lose the rule with nothing in the markup
// to say why. That is Section.astro's argument and it holds here too.
//
// The lede is the entry's `description` on the three article routes — the
// same string the index row and the meta description use
// (specs/content-model.md §3.1). `max-inline-[56ch]` is the archetype's lede
// measure, the same one Standing.astro pins on the index pages.
//
// Whatever follows the lede is the caller's: the meta line on the two writing
// routes, the stack chips plus the destination links on a case study, the
// review date on /colophon/, nothing at all on /about/.
//
// ── placement ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `hasContents` puts the header across both columns on row 1 of the article
// grid; see ArticleGrid.astro for the whole layout. It defaults to false, and
// that default is what /about/ and /colophon/ rely on: they render this header
// outside any grid, so the placement utilities must not be emitted on them at
// all. `min-[900px]:col-span-full` compiles to `grid-column: 1 / -1`, the
// exact declaration the stylesheet wrote; `min-[900px]:row-start-1` leaves
// grid-row-end at its initial value, which is what the `grid-row: 1`
// shorthand did.
//
// Both are named here in their prefixed form on purpose. Tailwind's scanner
// reads these comments, and the unprefixed spelling of either would emit a
// second rule that nothing on the site uses (verdict §4.4).

interface Props {
  /** The page's only h1. Plain text. */
  title: string;
  /** The one-sentence standfirst under it. Plain text. */
  lede: string;
  /**
   * True only inside an ArticleGrid whose article earned a contents list.
   * False (the default) means this header is not a grid item at all.
   */
  hasContents?: boolean;
}

const { title, lede, hasContents = false } = Astro.props;
---

<header
  class:list={[
    'mbe-12 pbe-8 border-be border-be-border',
    hasContents && 'min-[900px]:col-span-full min-[900px]:row-start-1',
  ]}
>
  <h1
    class="font-display text-size-h1 font-bold leading-display tracking-display text-text-strong"
  >{title}</h1>
  <p class="mbs-5 text-size-lede leading-tight text-muted max-inline-[56ch]">{lede}</p>
  <slot />
</header>
